  "body": "Stacked on #961 (branch `issue/869-coolant-air`). Retarget/merge after #961.\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe document's Units choice (`SetUnits`, already undoable and saved as `units`) is now also the unit every post writes the program in. One setting: the machine file's `units.length` no longer chooses anything; it only says what unit the file's own numbers are in.\n\n- **Seam.** The app adds `Units: \"mm\" | \"inch\"` to `postOptions` on every post path (whole program, per-operation files, per-mount files) via `posting::program_options`. The stream stays mm. `post.exe` takes `--units mm|inch`.\n- **Manifest law (`post::units`).** A script that can write inch declares `programUnits = \"mm inch\"`. An inch document on a script that doesn't is refused by name before any hook runs. This includes a user's own pre-#902 script. An unknown unit word is refused too.\n- **Posts that write inch:** Fanuc, Haas, Mazak and Doosan DNM (G20), and Siemens 840D (G700, the G710 twin). Lengths are written / 25.4 at four decimals and feeds in in/min at two. Angles, seconds and rpm are unchanged. The macro probe checks' band is one output step. The three Tormach posts now take the unit from the document instead of `machine.units`.\n- **Posts that refuse inch by name:** Makera Carvera (its firmware is mm only), Heidenhain (#976) and Fanuc Lathe (#977). For Heidenhain and Fanuc Lathe, inch output needs verified dialect work, not a guess.\n- **Old projects post byte-identical.** `PROJECT_VERSION` is now 59. A file at v58 or older opens on the unit its programs used to post in, taken from its machine files. If that differs from its saved display unit, a load note explains the change. A file whose setups posted in mixed units keeps its display unit, and a note names each setup whose unit changes.\n- **UI.** The Post section (document/setup Post page) gets a \"Program units\" mm / inch row. It is the same `SetUnits` as the Stock page's Units row, now shared code. The post status line names the unit.\n- **MCP.** New `set_units` tool (one undo step). `get_job` reports `units`.\n- Docs: `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` and `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` (the `Units` word, the `programUnits` manifest). Decisions: `docs/decisions/902-document-units.md`.\n\n**Behaviour change / breaking:** a new document on an inch machine file now posts mm until the document is set to inch. This covers every shipped Tormach machine. Older builds refuse v59 project files.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests (new):\n- `crates/app/tests/program_units.rs`\n  - `every_inch_post_writes_the_mm_program_in_inches`: 6 posts × 8 mill goldens. Each inch program is checked word by word against the same post's mm program: the unit word swaps, lengths are / 25.4, feeds are / 25.4, and every other word is equal. The unit word comes before the first motion. `Units: \"mm\"` is byte-identical to no unit at all. Inch goldens are committed under `golden/nc/inch/<post>/` (contour_plate_with_hole, drill_peck).\n  - `a_post_that_cannot_write_inch_refuses_the_document_by_name` (Carvera, Heidenhain, Fanuc Lathe)\n  - `a_script_that_declares_no_units_refuses_inch_and_posts_mm`\n  - `no_shipped_post_takes_the_program_unit_from_the_machine_file`\n  - `an_inch_machine_file_no_longer_makes_an_inch_program`\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_units.rs::the_document_unit_is_the_posted_unit_through_undo_and_save` covers the end-to-end path over MCP: a Fanuc face job posts G21; `set_units` inch posts G20 with X / 25.4; Carvera refuses by name; save and reopen keep inch; undo gives back the identical mm program. Also `set_units_refuses_nonsense_and_no_ops`.\n- `crates/app/tests/units_migrate.rs` (5 tests): the v58 → v59 rung in four cases (inch machine, inch display on a metric machine, matching display, mixed-unit setups), plus a v59 file that keeps its unit whatever the machine.\n- `crates/post/src/post/units.rs` unit tests (unit word, manifest law).\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/program_units.rs::the_post_page_sets_the_program_unit_through_set_units`\n\nUpdated: the Tormach, plasma, microARC, probe and Carvera suites. Before this change, several of them used \"an inch machine file\" to mean \"an inch program\". Each now states an inch document instead: `SetUnits` in world tests, `Units` in engine tests. Their goldens are unchanged. `carvera_post::an_inch_machine_is_refused_by_name` became `an_inch_document_is_refused_by_name`. It now also pins that an inch machine file alone still posts G21.\n\n**Goldens:** no existing golden moved; the mm output is byte-identical (conformance and every post suite green). New: 12 inch goldens under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/`.\n\nGate (Linux): `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/869-coolant-air` green: post, app (every app suite, since a shared test helper changed) and ui suites, 10.2 min, 0 failed. `.cps` changes are not gate-mapped (#923), but the whole app set ran, which covers every post suite (conformance, the per-post suites, post_unit_word). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No hand test on a real control in inch.\n- Sinumerik G700 rests on the published G710/G700 pairing. It has not been run on an 840D.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill's tool table (`.claude/skills/`, a process file) is not updated with `set_units`. That needs a PROCESS_VERSION bump, so it is left for the maintainer.\n- Overlap: #258 (Post dialog, in review) touches the same post section UI.\n- Found while testing, not caused here: #978 (MCP `open_project` over a non-empty document duplicates its operations).\n\nChangelog: Program units are a document setting: every post writes the program in the document's mm/inch (G21/G20, 840D G710/G700), never the machine file's; Carvera, Heidenhain and Fanuc Lathe refuse an inch document by name; older projects open on the unit they posted in; MCP `set_units`.\n\nCommit type: `feat(post)!` (BREAKING CHANGE footer; under 0.x it bumps MINOR).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #902\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
